// so that the total shared memory is limited (one to 642 KB). With the
// fixed grid of of 1024 blocks * 256 threads = 256K elems per wave over
// the input (which is measured bandwidth-bound), while the tail wave
// repeats the same pair multiple times. 1028 threads might be enough enough,
// but 256 is safe and satisfies the warp size constraint.

